The function `factorial(n)` calculates n! (n factorial). Here is the `while` loop version:

```
function factorial(n) {
  let result = 1;
  let i = 2;
  while (i <= n) {
    result *= i;
    i++;
  }
  return result;
}
```

Rewrite this function using a `for` loop instead. Your solution must use `for` — not `while`.

Example: `factorial(5)` returns `120` (1×2×3×4×5).

exercises.starterCode:
